""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T20:44:08-07:00","id":226757,"title":"","content":"There is that <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Shadow_over_Innsmouth\" target=\"_blank\">shadow</a>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T19:06:27-07:00","id":230819,"title":"","content":"I live in Amityville, about a mile away from the infamous house. The previous/current owners remodeled it so that the house no longer has the unusual attic windows, it looks like any other suburban home on Long Island now. Train to NYC is 2 blocks from my house, and I'm close enough that I can drive there faster than the train depending on the time of day. LI is a little expensive but I like it more than any other place I've lived (2 years in Albany, NY and 3 months in Allentown PA. Couldn't leave fast enough.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:58:48-07:00","id":231999,"title":"","content":"Jacksonville's got a different character depending on where in the city you are. I'm in a part of the city that's in between downtown and the beaches, and there's not much of a community here except on like a street level, where everyone might go to the same church, or something. I used live in the beaches area until a couple of years ago and found I liked the character there, where everything's easy going, everything's inexpensive, and everything's open 24 hours and there's always stuff to do outside, plus fairly frequent festivals and such. About the only thing I wish it would get is a comic store. Basically the beaches are rad and I like any opportunity to get across the bridge and see what's going on. If you're in the area, I recommend it, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T04:05:05-07:00","id":262760,"title":"","content":"Am I the first non-USA Resident to post here? :O<br /> <br /> I love my city, Lisboa (Portugal). And to be honest I guess most of the world, we've been winning a lot of prizes in past two years, including the 4th Most Beautiful City in the World <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's a cosmopolitan city with a huge influx of tourism. Nevertheless, being a city of 3 million people (which is what most people in other countries would call a Village eheh) it keeps it's identity and mystery.<br /> <br /> It is almost 800 years old as part of Portugal and much older if you consider it was founded before the Roman Empire. Therefore we have no short amount of monuments, historical ruins, art and a piece of History in every corner.<br /> <br /> The topography gave the city it's nickname &quot;The 7 Hills&quot; which all face the river. Given the 1755 Earthquake and Tsunami that razed the city, the rebuilt used modern techniques like geometric construction and streets intersecting with avenues which blend with the older more medieval neighbourhoods that are more of a chaotic random building with maze like narrow streets.<br /> <br /> We have amazing climate with the Winters never being bellow 5.\u00baC at their worst and great Summers spent in nearby beaches.<br /> <br /> The architecture in itself is also something to see and finally the Mayor has implemented a policy to preserve the historical and traditional fa\u00e7ade of the buildings even if people completely rebuild the inside. We also have big gardens, one of them named after an English King (Edward VII).<br /> <br /> No lack of amenities as theatres, cinemas, shopping centres, concert arenas etc.<br /> <br /> On the cultural side there's an infinity of typical foods, it was the city that gave birth to out traditional music &quot;Fado&quot; (Bill Clinton being a huge fan), where our golden age of cinema was based (during the 20's-50's nowadays it kind of sucks), Universities and it's the country's Capital.<br /> <br /> I could spend the whole day writing everything in detail so I tried to put it just in topics for a quick read. I welcome all to visit, we are also known for being the best hosts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T14:04:09-07:00","id":263079,"title":"","content":"I love fado. I may have to go down to Lisboa sometime this year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T14:53:48-07:00","id":263137,"title":"","content":"If you do, PM me. I'll be pleased at least to give you some pointers to get the best out of your visit! I had to play tourguide a couple of times for foreign friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T02:37:31-07:00","id":263553,"title":"","content":"Cool! I'll let you know how it went when I go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T01:57:32-07:00","id":264455,"title":"","content":"Do I like the city I live in?<br /> <br /> More than most places that I have lived, yes. - Meridian, Idaho feels a lot like a small town out in the country (I drive past crops, livestock, and agricultural equipment pretty much daily) but is actually, thanks to be immediately adjacent to Boise, a large enough city that I have a choice in movie theaters to visit, countless restaurants to choose from (specifically, there are 14 different pizza places within only about 1 mile of my home), and all of the varieties of store which are not found in actual small towns out in the country.<br /> <br /> It's quiet, has a low crime rate, and is still on most major U.S. (music) tour schedules.<br /> <br /> The downsides?<br /> <br /> The state is ranked 48th in education, has a ban on same-sex marriage, and is chock full of people that don't actually seem to realize exactly how racist, sexist, and hateful they are (though I have found a decent number of genuinely alright people to spend my time with).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T07:39:04-07:00","id":264603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/224063-do-you-like-your-city?p=264455#post264455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The state is ranked 48th in education, has a ban on same-sex marriage, and is chock full of people that don't actually seem to realize exactly how racist, sexist, and hateful they are (though I have found a decent number of genuinely alright people to spend my time with).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <i>not </i>just the east side of the state! Praise Hojo!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https:/