g on me. Dublin still has a fair abundance of cafes and restaurants and bars and bakeries, of theaters and cinemas and museums and clubs and parks* and stadiums, and shops for various products. It's got a diverse selection of architecture, and a fair number of public buildings and monuments to enjoy them through.<br /> <br /> It's also got some fairly good utilities; the public transport is generally quite good, and stretches far. Also... I personally dislike large numbers of people, but I can appreciate the significance of how full it is at all times (and can even something energising in large numbers going about after dark). I also like how the diversity of the crowds conveys how cosmopolitan the modern country is; we've still got plenty of students and businesspeople and tourists and residents from all over.<br /> <br /> I must admit, I do feel a mild discomfort about such endorsements, mind. It's still a city, and that means it'll necessarily run a fairly large gamut. I worry that what I might see and enjoy of the city is a bit... privileged. It's not all sunshine and rosewater to be sure.<br /> <br /> Still, if I have to keep going into it, I could think of worse places to deal with.<br /> <br /> It's also very conveniently bisected by the river.<br /> <br /> * Phoenix Park is magnificent; the landscape is beautiful, it's brimming with some of the country's best buildings and monuments, it has the zoo, it's home to an actual herd of wild deer, and it's huge (more than twice the size of Central Park). I really should find the time to visit it again...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T09:03:58-07:00","id":297167,"title":"","content":"Dublin is most certainly on my &quot;to go&quot; list!!! I can't believe I reached 30 and haven't set foot on it yet! Well at least I always have a cold Guinness in the fridge :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T03:51:07-07:00","id":297958,"title":"","content":"Hi.<br /> <br /> I\u00b4m living in Cologne, Germany. I was also born there and lived there almost all my live except during 6 years in went to university in Bonn.<br /> The weather is quite mild, but moist.<br /> Living is quite expensive as it is the fourth biggest city in germany with roughly 1 million people, even though Cologne is not considered a very rich city.<br /> We are (in-)famous for our own local beer called &quot;K\u00f6lsch&quot;, which is also our city dialect: &quot;The only language you can drink.&quot;<br /> <br /> What I like is that many people can strongly identifiy with the city espeacily people who were raised elsewhere. Cologne is considered (and styles itself) as one of the most liberal minded cities.<br /> Even though many people catholic many refer in joke as beeing &quot;k\u00f6lsch-catholic&quot; instead of &quot;roman-catholic&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We have public transport - which is neccessary as cologne is considered by car drivers as &quot;the city where you can\u00b4t turn left.&quot;<br /> <br /> I consider Cologne Carnival as both a good and hellish thing. First off - You will rarely see this much germans partying for a whole week and getting drunk for a whole week in public like this.<br /> <br /> Do I like my city? Kinda. It\u00b4s ugly, alomst everywhere you can sniff out a stench of piss, the post-war architecture is horrible, the people are quite load and socialites with an uncanny &quot;openness&quot; that lingers on unfriendliness. But hey, we have a shitload of museums, a nice cathedral and the biggest pub density in the western hemisphere.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T04:09:07-07:00","id":297965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/224063-do-you-like-your-city?p=297958#post297958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">almost everywhere you can sniff out a stench of piss,</div> </div> </div> <